# CASP15 H1172 — The Full Machine (7PBP)
---

And now the complete assembly.

This is RuvB with two copies of the RuvA domain —
the full DNA repair machine captured
in its working state.

Also from the Nature 2022 paper by Wald
and colleagues.

> close
> load 7pbp
---

With two RuvA domains bound, we can see
the complete architecture of this
molecular machine.

The two RuvA domains sit on opposite faces
of the RuvB hexamer, creating a channel
through which DNA is threaded.

> spin 0.15
---

The ATP molecules drive the whole assembly.

As they're hydrolyzed one by one around
the ring, the RuvB motor pulls DNA
through at about 50 base pairs per second —
fast enough to repair a Holliday junction
before it causes problems.

> stop
> view ligand
---

From T1170 to H1171 to H1172, CASP15 presented
this system in increasing complexity —
first the motor alone, then with one partner,
then the full machine.

A brilliant way to test prediction methods
at every level of biological organization.

> reset
> spin 0.1
---

The complete RuvAB machine — nature's
DNA junction resolver.
PDB code 7PBP, CASP15 target H1172.

> stop
